<title>NORWAY: FORECAST-Christiania 1996 profit seen down.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Christiania 1996 profit seen down.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse ASA, Norway's second biggest commercial bank, is forecast to post 1996 pre-tax operating profits of 1.86 billion crowns, down from 2.79 billion in 1996, according to seven analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>Two said buy, four said hold and one said sell the share, which closed at 23.30 crowns on the Oslo Bourse on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bank announced on December 31 that 228 million crowns earmarked for severance and other payments linked to planned staff reductions would burden the 1996 accounts.</p>
<p>The bank plans to reduce staff by nine percent, or 390 people, in the next two years. The slimming down of operations will lead to an annual cost reduction of an estimated 130 million crowns, according to the bank.</p>
<p>Christiania will present the annual result on February 19</p>
<p>				   (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>						   Expectations	 1995</p>
